-- title:
--   Group averaging, word sectors, cyclic restriction and letter pullback for representations
-- statement:
--   Four general constructions for complex representations, used to move nonzero equivariant maps between related modules.
--
--   Let $G$ be a group and let $\rho$, $\sigma$ be representations of $G$ on complex vector spaces $X$, $Y$. For $v\in X$ write $\langle v\rangle_\rho=\operatorname{span}_{\mathbb{C}}\{\rho(g)v: g\in G\}$ for the cyclic subrepresentation generated by $v$. For $n,d\in\mathbb{N}$ write $[n]=\{0,1,\dots,n-1\}$ and let $M_{n,d}$ be the complex vector space of functions $x:[d]^{[n]}\to\mathbb{C}$ on words $w:[n]\to[d]$ (positions $[n]$, letters $[d]$), with indicator vectors $\delta_w$; the symmetric group $\mathfrak S_n$ acts by $(g\cdot x)(w)=x(w\circ g)$, so that $g\cdot\delta_w=\delta_{w\circ g^{-1}}$.
--
--   1. **Group averaging.** If $G$ is finite and $f:X\to Y$ is any linear map, then
--   $$
--   \operatorname{Av}(f)=\sum_{g\in G}\sigma(g)\circ f\circ\rho(g^{-1})
--   $$
--   is a $G$-equivariant linear map $X\to Y$, i.e. an intertwiner from $\rho$ to $\sigma$.
--
--   2. **Word sectors.** For a set $D\subseteq[n]$ of positions and a set $A\subseteq[d]$ of letters, a word $w:[n]\to[d]$ lies in the sector $(D,A)$ when, for every position $i$, $w(i)\in A$ holds if and only if $i\in D$; that is, the letters from $A$ occur exactly at the positions in $D$.
--
--   3. **Restriction to cyclic subrepresentations.** An intertwiner $F$ from $\rho$ to $\sigma$ maps $\langle v\rangle_\rho$ into $\langle F(v)\rangle_\sigma$, because $F(\rho(g)v)=\sigma(g)F(v)$; the restricted map $\langle v\rangle_\rho\to\langle F(v)\rangle_\sigma$ is an intertwiner between the restricted representations.
--
--   4. **Pulling back letters.** For a map of alphabets $\varphi:[d]\to[D]$, the map $M_{n,D}\to M_{n,d}$,
--   $$
--   x\longmapsto\big(w\mapsto x(\varphi\circ w)\big),
--   $$
--   is an $\mathfrak S_n$-intertwiner. When $\varphi$ is injective it reads off the coefficients of the words written in the sub-alphabet $\varphi([d])$.
--
--   Averaging turns maps that are equivariant only for a subgroup into genuinely equivariant ones, word sectors describe the coordinate supports against which such averages are tested, and the cyclic restriction and letter pullback transport nonzero intertwiners between cyclic modules generated by related vectors.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The constructions are `averagedMap ρ σ f` (which requires `[Fintype G]`), `wordSector D A` (with `D : Fin n → Prop` and `A : Fin d → Prop`), `cyclicMap F v` (obtained by `codRestrict` from the membership lemma `intertwiner_cyclic_mem`) and `restrictLetters φ`. Intertwiners are `Representation.IntertwiningMap`s and $\langle v\rangle_\rho$ is `cyclic ρ v`.
